        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "749b6c17-6a27-3e7a-b80f-f8a5308c4b30",
                "word": "géomancie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "bd8cf7dc-05d8-4e81-b715-36e6517bc997",
                        "entry_id": "749b6c17-6a27-3e7a-b80f-f8a5308c4b30",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "géomancies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6dc312a2-a61b-383d-827b-59b01928ca3f",
                        "entry_id": "749b6c17-6a27-3e7a-b80f-f8a5308c4b30",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Divination de l’avenir ou des choses secrètes par des points que l’on marque au hasard sur la terre ou sur du papier, que l’on réunit par des lignes, et dont on observe ensuite le nombre ou la situation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a1589ad-00f0-4cc4-99f5-eb9a5ca2e03f",
                                "sense_id": "6dc312a2-a61b-383d-827b-59b01928ca3f",
                                "text": "Figure de géomancie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94344bd8-2f6a-4024-8a0e-25aef697d612",
                                "sense_id": "6dc312a2-a61b-383d-827b-59b01928ca3f",
                                "text": "Il [l’Inquisiteur-général Manrique de Lara] dépêcha en Biscaye l’inquisiteur de Calahorra pour qu’il y conduise une enquête minutieuse et établisse la liste des pratiques magiques et des superstitions suspectes : esprits familiers et actes sacrilèges, astrologie judiciaire, géomancie, hydromancie, pyromancie, aéromancie et nécromancie sans oublier la divination par les ongles, l’on[ych]omancie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "686b1d5e-9c46-4928-b558-b96b18ddd2b8",
                                "sense_id": "6dc312a2-a61b-383d-827b-59b01928ca3f",
                                "text": "Les tempéraments sanguins sont plus disposés à l’aéromancie, les bilieux à la pyromancie, les pituiteux à l’hydromancie, et les mélancoliques à la géomancie. L’aéromancie se confirme par l’onéiromancie ou divination par les songes ; on supplée à la pyromancie par le magnétisme, à l’hydromancie par la cristallomancie, et à la géomancie par la cartomancie. Ce sont des transpositions et des perfectionnements de méthodes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8cc082f-7832-466d-ba9b-62a686ce1e8a",
                                "sense_id": "6dc312a2-a61b-383d-827b-59b01928ca3f",
                                "text": "Ayant acquis aussi des connaissances profondes du taoïsme, il était très versé dans la géomancie et l’art divinatoire."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e2eb812-10e7-3925-a634-2026eb330d2a",
                        "entry_id": "749b6c17-6a27-3e7a-b80f-f8a5308c4b30",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Méthode de divination qui consiste à interpréter les dessins faits par de la terre jetée sur une surface plane."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ba23cff9-922b-410b-bd63-71268cb2707a",
                        "source_entry_id": "749b6c17-6a27-3e7a-b80f-f8a5308c4b30",
                        "target_lang_word": "Geomantie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9c085471-647d-4b10-a13b-574ed49d3bc1",
                        "source_entry_id": "749b6c17-6a27-3e7a-b80f-f8a5308c4b30",
                        "target_lang_word": "Geomantik",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2fd4a043-d3a0-4fca-bd7c-44f82ffdcc2b",
                        "source_entry_id": "749b6c17-6a27-3e7a-b80f-f8a5308c4b30",
                        "target_lang_word": "geomancy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "geomancy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f8328a6-5190-3d6b-bbd3-43e5e7a61916",
                                        "entry_id": "8c4527b5-4dcb-3d4a-9046-a601f489a66a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A method of divination using earth or the ground, such as interpreting markings on the ground or how handfuls of dirt land when tossed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38f0a2b0-9287-4f12-9322-9b45694b14ea",
                                                "sense_id": "9f8328a6-5190-3d6b-bbd3-43e5e7a61916",
                                                "text": "1660 Urquhart tr. Rabelais Gargantua & Pantagruel iii. xxv.\nHard by here, in the Brown-wheat-Island, dwelleth Her Trippa; you know how by the Arts of Astrology, Geomancy, Chiromancy, Metopomancy, and others of a like stuff and nature, he foretelleth all things to come..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a1102ea-fec5-480e-8581-26926bde1a39",
                                                "sense_id": "9f8328a6-5190-3d6b-bbd3-43e5e7a61916",
                                                "text": "The Arabian Geomancy, said to have been first practised by Almadul, was more recondite, being founded on the effects of motion under the crust of the earth, the chinks thus produced, and the noises or thunderings heard; its foundation was the dogma of Aristotle, that \"the moving of the heaven is everlasting, and is the beginning and cause of all inferior movings.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7d64d93-b020-4a9d-85fc-57785b2197a1",
                                                "sense_id": "9f8328a6-5190-3d6b-bbd3-43e5e7a61916",
                                                "text": "In geomancy, the enquirer himself was asked to stab the earth at random with a pointed stick. The soothsayer then read the dots."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65a48090-b0ca-455b-ac55-d17db32d45f5",
                                                "sense_id": "9f8328a6-5190-3d6b-bbd3-43e5e7a61916",
                                                "text": "The fountain or the well represents a point where invisible energies flow into a society; in geomancy these would be known as \"power points.\" Where these energies are, elementals or genii loci or nature spirits congregate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9496004-090e-3837-99bc-67f16da0766a",
                                        "entry_id": "8c4527b5-4dcb-3d4a-9046-a601f489a66a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "feng shui; Chinese geomancy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd9f9db5-0478-4606-a84f-b72a042df8eb",
                                                "sense_id": "f9496004-090e-3837-99bc-67f16da0766a",
                                                "text": "geomancy [...] The pretended art of divining future events, or of ascertaining the luckiness or unluckiness of any event or locality, by means of signs connected with the earth [...] or, as in China, from the configuration and aspect of a particular region in its relation to some other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b8b3e13-036e-42d3-955c-e4cb912973a3",
                                                "sense_id": "f9496004-090e-3837-99bc-67f16da0766a",
                                                "text": "There was [...] a striking similarity between Mesopotamian and Chinese thinking - if not method - in the concept of feng-shui, the Chinese system of geomancy, or divination by topographical features."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb733ca2-b5a7-4c5c-b1c8-0d1afeb739dd",
                                                "sense_id": "f9496004-090e-3837-99bc-67f16da0766a",
                                                "text": "You realize we all live in our surroundings, and you start to look at your surroundings through Feng Shui and geomancy, and try to see, if we understand ourselves and others, how can we make our surroundings as good as they can be for us and the others."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
